  "method": "Same reader and cleaning rules as town_days.json (EIA adjusted demand; demand hours flagged as implausible are left out). Relative error e = (actual demand - day-ahead forecast) / forecast; positive e means demand came in above the forecast. January-April only: from May 2025 the day-ahead forecast SPP reports to EIA averages 8-15% above its reported demand in every month (monthly_forecast_ratio). The cause is unverified: a reporting or definition mismatch between the two series is possible, and leaving May-December out is an editorial choice pending validation. EIA-930 instructions let a balancing authority report the day-ahead forecast it makes in the normal course of business even when it is not defined exactly like reported demand. Persistence baselines: demand in the same hour one day (lag 24 h) or one week (lag 168 h) earlier, over the same valid hours. Wind persistence: |w(t) - w(t-L)| over hours where both values are valid, divided by the 2025 maximum hourly wind output.",
